# --- P0-4: www  -- DO NOT PUT THIS RULE IN THIS FILE -------------------------
# Status 2026-08-22: DNS is fixed (www resolves, TLS covers *.core-asset-sol.com)
# but the redirect is BROKEN. It emits a literal, uninterpolated ":splat":
#
#     https://www.core-asset-sol.com/contact
#       -> 301 -> https://core-asset-sol.com/:splat  -> 404
#
# Every www URL, whatever the path, lands on the same 404.
#
# Root cause: ":splat" is Netlify / Cloudflare Pages _redirects syntax. It means
# nothing in a Cloudflare Redirect Rule, whose wildcard replacement syntax is
# ${1} / ${2}. Cloudflare treated ":splat" as a literal string and copied it into
# the Location header verbatim.
#
# The rule is running as a Cloudflare Redirect Rule at the edge, not through
# Pages - the response has no cf-cache-status and no access-control-allow-origin,
# so it never reaches this file.
#
# It cannot live in this file either way: Cloudflare Pages does not support
# domain-level redirects in _redirects, because _redirects cannot match on
# hostname. Attempting "/*  https://core-asset-sol.com/:splat  301" here would
# also match apex requests and cause an infinite redirect loop.
#
# CORRECT FIX - Cloudflare dashboard > zone > Rules > Redirect Rules.
# Using the Wildcard pattern mode the dashboard defaults to:
#
#     When incoming requests match -> Wildcard pattern
#       Request URL:  http*://www.core-asset-sol.com/*
#     Then
#       Target URL:   https://core-asset-sol.com/${2}
#       Status code:  301
#       Preserve query string: Enabled
#
# WATCH THE NUMBERING. ${1}/${2} refer to the asterisks in the Request URL, in
# order. In the pattern above the first * is the "s" in http*, so the PATH is
# the SECOND capture:
#     https://www.core-asset-sol.com/*   -> 1 wildcard  -> path is ${1}
#     http*://www.core-asset-sol.com/*   -> 2 wildcards -> path is ${2}
#
# The leading http*:// also matches port 80, which fixes the separate 522 error
# on http://www.core-asset-sol.com/. Confirm the www DNS record is proxied
# (orange cloud), not DNS-only.
#
# Equivalent using the expression editor instead:
#     If:    (http.host eq "www.core-asset-sol.com")
#     Then:  type = Dynamic
#            expression = concat("https://core-asset-sol.com", http.request.uri.path)
#
# Verify:
#     curl -sSI https://www.core-asset-sol.com/contact | grep -iE '^(HTTP|location)'
#     -> want: 301 and location: https://core-asset-sol.com/contact
#        NOT /:splat, NOT /${2}, NOT a bare /

